Wed Aug 26 2026 Anton Isaiev <totoshko88@gmail.com> - 0.20.9
- Version bump to 0.20.9
- Added: a connection can take its jump host from its group or from the
  application — three tiers are consulted, nearest first: the connection's own
  Jump Host, then the group chain, then a new Settings → Connection → Network
  group holding a Global Jump Host and a Global ProxyJump. A new Network Mode
  row on the editor's Basic page chooses between "Inherit from group or global"
  and "Direct" — on Basic rather than on the SSH page because the choice
  applies to every protocol and the protocol pages show only one at a time;
  rustconn-cli gained --network-mode inherit|direct (issue #301)
- Added: the external RDP client can be told how to size its window — a new
  External Window row in the editor's Display group offers Fit to screen (the
  default), Fullscreen, Custom resolution and All monitors. It governs both the
  External client mode and the window an embedded session hands over to when
  IronRDP cannot serve the server; rustconn-cli gained --rdp-display-mode and
  --rdp-resolution
- Fixed: an external RDP window opened at about a quarter of a 4K screen — the
  size handed to FreeRDP came from the embedded viewer's own widget geometry in
  logical pixels. Every RDP profile also stored a 1920x1080 resolution nobody
  chose, which that path then applied; a connection that deliberately used a
  fixed size needs Custom resolution selected once
- Fixed: External client mode ignored an RD Gateway completely and never
  filtered custom FreeRDP arguments, while Display Scale and Color Depth were
  collected from every connection and emitted by nobody. The three argument
  builders are now the single one in rustconn-core
- Fixed: a group's Jump Host was never used — the picker stored the choice and
  showed it again when reopened, but nothing read it at connect time. Two
  further defects in the same dialog: a group configured with only a jump host
  opened with the SSH switch off and threw the host away on the next save, and
  the bastion rows were hidden until an authentication method was chosen
  (issue #301)
- Fixed: whether a connection inherited its proxy depended on where it got its
  SSH key — the group chain was walked only when the key source was "Inherit
  from group", which made a group bastion and a connection-level key file
  mutually exclusive, while RDP, VNC and SPICE inherited unconditionally with
  no way to refuse. Inheritance now keys off Network Mode and reads the same
  for every protocol
- Fixed: rustconn-cli group set --ssh-proxy-jump "" produced ssh -J "" — an
  empty value now clears the setting, for --ssh-agent-socket too, and a blank
  counts as unset at all three tiers, the hand-editable global one included
- Fixed: a pinned connection's real row never updated — a pinned connection is
  in the sidebar twice and the four update walkers stopped at the first match,
  so the row in its group or at the root had no status icon, recording dot,
  external-viewer emblem or split marker, and its context menu offered Connect
  for a session that was already open (issue #302)
- Fixed: the recording dot, the external-viewer emblem and the split marker
  vanished on any sidebar reload — a rename, a duplicate, a pin toggle, a
  re-sort or a drag-drop cleared them until the next session event
- Fixed: the Simplified Chinese translation has never loaded, in any package —
  every install path derives the locale directory from the catalogue filename,
  so zh-cn.po was installed to share/locale/zh-cn/ while gettext looks up
  zh_CN. The catalogue is now po/zh_CN.po and a stored zh-cn language choice
  keeps working
- Fixed: Settings populated its connection dropdowns before it was given the
  connection list, so the startup-action picker had nothing to choose
- Changed: the sidebar's "Open new session" is offered whenever there is a
  session to duplicate, not only for external-viewer sessions (issue #302)
- Changed: a server that runs RDS licensing is named as such instead of
  "incompatible" — the session still falls back to the external FreeRDP
  client, which connects; the cause is upstream (IronRDP #1629)
- Changed: an OpenH264 library that is installed but refused now says why —
  the loader compares its SHA-256 against the binaries Cisco itself publishes,
  so no distribution build can pass. RUSTCONN_OPENH264 names a library to try
  before anything else
- Improved: every Secret Service call has a deadline, not just the GUI's whole
  credential resolution — rustconn-cli had no bound at all and could wait
  forever on a locked keyring
- Improved: the ProxyJump row's subtitle names the bastion a connection has
  inherited, or says that Direct is ignoring one
- Packaging: the rpmlint errors on the OBS build are cleared — the Summary is
  within the 79-character limit, %find_lang generates the locale file list, and
  Requires on libadwaita and libasound2 are gone since rpm derives both from
  the linked binary. A %check section runs the rustconn-core suites
- Localisation: Simplified Chinese now loads; 13 new strings translated in all
  17 locales
- Dependencies: combine 4.6.7→4.6.8
